# pll-drift-clamp-fixed.patch  (RECOMMENDED over pll-drift-clamp.patch)
#
# STATUS: implemented, compiles, NOT yet confirmed by an A/B measurement. The
# defect it corrects was reproduced by measurement; the benefit of the clamp
# itself was not. One part is CURRENTLY UNTESTABLE: the re-lock on screen change
# needs two monitors, and the machine has one at the moment.
#
# Same idea as pll-drift-clamp.patch - anchor the estimated period to the
# interval the display reports, +/-1% - with three differences:
#
#  1. The reference rate comes from the screen the render window is ACTUALLY on
#     (VSyncThread::setDisplayRefreshRate, fed by WaveformWidgetFactory), not
#     from the primary screen. The as-built version pins the period to the wrong
#     screen on a multi-monitor setup: a window on a 120 Hz panel next to a
#     60 Hz primary was measured running at 60 fps because of it.
#  2. It follows the window: QWindow::screenChanged re-reports the rate, and a
#     change RE-LOCKS the loop from scratch. Merely re-clamping would leave a
#     period from the new screen with a phase from the old one. (Untested - no
#     second monitor available right now.)
#  3. When the rate is unknown (QScreen::refreshRate() returns 0 on some
#     platforms), the plausibility check and the clamp are both disabled instead
#     of running against a garbage value; the median initialisation is
#     self-sufficient.
#
# NOT COMBINABLE with display-link.patch (same regions, neither order applies).
#
# Requires: pll-init-fix-fixed.patch applied first - it provides the rejection
# timeout this builds on. Mutually exclusive with pll-drift-clamp.patch.
diff --git a/src/waveform/vsyncthread.cpp b/src/waveform/vsyncthread.cpp
index e66ae7f004..5c2c743246 100644
--- a/src/waveform/vsyncthread.cpp
+++ b/src/waveform/vsyncthread.cpp
@@ -16,14 +16,21 @@ constexpr int kNumStableDeltasRequired = 20;
